          "When customer success work scales, escalation log becomes a coordination problem: several people can touch the same request without anyone seeing the full sequence of source, decision, action, and confirmation. Without a visible owner, the request can sit in a shared inbox while everyone assumes someone else has checked the renewal forecast. Treat the escalation log as a closed loop rather than a message: every action needs a source, a boundary, a destination, and a time. A queue that mixes new requests with corrections will overstate demand and understate the time spent repairing earlier work. The escalation log review at Customer Success Managers should state whether the escalation record was current on October 28."
