          "Do not treat a forwarded email as the record itself when the governing value lives in the CRM; the email may explain intent, but it does not replace the field. For recurring escalation log work, use the same renewal risk memo type and the same field labels so a sample can be compared across owners. If the renewal risk memo is incomplete, the safest next step may be to pause escalation log rather than fill the gap with a plausible assumption. If the renewal risk memo contains personal or confidential data, use the approved access path and record only the reference in the queue. The October 28 escalation log note should distinguish a missing renewal risk memo from a confirmed negative.",
          "Record the usage report and the time it was observed, because a later screenshot cannot prove what the record said when the first action was taken. When the usage report is missing, write missing rather than leaving the field blank; missing, unavailable, and confirmed negative are different states. After the conflict is resolved, add a short correction entry to the escalation log log and link it to both source versions. Keep the usage report in the approved repository and link it to the escalation log case instead of attaching it to a personal message. At Customer Success Managers, record the October 28 escalation log correction and link it to the original source."
