          "The operator can make the usage report usable, but should not invent the rationale for an approval that CSM never gave. Do not let urgency expand the role; if the request affects incomplete onboarding, the boundary stays in place even when the deadline is tight. The approval record should point to the usage report that was reviewed, not only to the request that started the work. If CSM delegates approval, record the delegate, the scope, the start time, and the end time. For the October 28 sample, Customer Success Managers should include one escalation log case that crossed owners."
