          "Before adding a new escalation log item, check whether the request already exists under another name or channel. At mid-day, check the escalation log items that have no next action; those are the ones most likely to age silently. Record any correction made during the day and link it to the original escalation log record. Use the same escalation log status values across owners so the daily count means the same thing to everyone. At Customer Success Managers, the October 28 escalation log review should name the backup owner and the coverage window.",
          "Open the escalation log queue in the support desk and mark every item with the current owner, the next action, and the time it is due. When the next step belongs to customer sponsor, write the request and the due time instead of leaving the case in a waiting state. Close the day by checking that each completed escalation log has a destination update in the support desk and a confirmation for the requester. A daily stand-up should review exceptions and aging items, not read every completed ticket aloud. The October 28 escalation log exception log should show the reason code, owner, and release decision."
